WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.390
Hi, I'm Gumdrop!

00:00:02.390 --> 00:00:06.791
XGrammar sits under SGLang and vLLM, and stops a model emitting a

00:00:06.791 --> 00:00:08.991
tool call your program can't parse.

00:00:08.991 --> 00:00:09.725
Here's how.

00:00:10.933 --> 00:00:14.789
The new part: the schema is separate from the wire syntax.

00:00:14.789 --> 00:00:19.696
One JSON description, compiled to a grammar that masks the vocabulary at every step.

00:00:21.050 --> 00:00:24.692
The caller declares a shape: a schema for the arguments, and begin

00:00:24.692 --> 00:00:26.817
and end markers for the wire format.

00:00:26.817 --> 00:00:28.942
The engine compiles it to a grammar.

00:00:29.362 --> 00:00:32.834
Masks are precomputed into a cache, so at decode time the common

00:00:32.834 --> 00:00:33.992
case is a lookup.

00:00:34.412 --> 00:00:38.872
At every step, a token that would leave the language gets zero probability.

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:40.931
The rest are renormalised and sampled.

00:00:41.351 --> 00:00:44.328
So there's no decode path to an invalid string.

00:00:44.328 --> 00:00:45.982
Not ninety-nine percent: a proof.

00:00:47.233 --> 00:00:50.238
A JSON-only decoder ties the schema to JSON.

00:00:50.238 --> 00:00:55.497
But DeepSeek V4 writes its tool calls as XML, with its own control tokens.

00:00:55.917 --> 00:01:00.905
Structural Tag keeps one schema and adds a style: nine wire formats, one library.

00:01:00.905 --> 00:01:05.181
Triggered tags let a model reason freely, then call a tool strictly.

00:01:06.383 --> 00:01:10.135
On the smallest Llama, the tag took schema accuracy from twenty-one

00:01:10.135 --> 00:01:11.500
percent to a hundred.

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:14.911
Output accuracy went from five to forty-six and a half.

00:01:16.017 --> 00:01:18.718
So a grammar's guarantee is unconditional, and narrow.

00:01:18.718 --> 00:01:20.068
The output always parses.

00:01:20.068 --> 00:01:23.106
Whether it's right is still up to the model.

00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:28.825
To recap: a tag becomes a grammar, the grammar masks tokens, and

00:01:28.825 --> 00:01:30.669
it guarantees parsing, not correctness.

00:01:31.089 --> 00:01:33.199
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:33.199 --> 00:01:33.801
I'm Gumdrop.

00:01:33.801 --> 00:01:34.103
Bye!
